Z||000011||BAM-BAM||04-08-2001||03:39 PM||||  This is classy!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Blackleather.JPG">  <P>Red is an awesome accent color. Using red as a base color is very tricky due to it's overpowering properties. I am also using red as an accent in my leather interior. If you can pull it off, you da man! Good luck!<BR>Here's a pic of my seats.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroseats2.JPG"> <P><BR>Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 04-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cozmo||04-08-2001||04:07 PM||||Right, BAM-BAM, red is a fussy color to do an interior with tastefully.  I used to have an MGB that was black with a red interior, it was quite striking...<BR>I can see where two-tone red/black or red/gray could work...<BR>Oh oh...the wheels are turning again... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>C02M0||||reg||3
